Data sources and attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FinEvents acquires data from third-party sources. Per ADR-0044:

  - Raw acquired content (scraped article text, exchange page content, and
    provider payloads) is NEVER redistributed by this project.

  - Derived work produced by this project — severity scores, wiki pages,
    predictions, scores, run manifests, calibration maps, and the steering
    audit trail — IS published, and is covered by the Apache License above.

  - Source URLs and fetch timestamps are published so that third parties may
    re-acquire source material under their own terms.

Per-source licences and attribution obligations are recorded in DATA_SOURCES.md.

GDELT Project data is licensed CC BY 4.0 and requires attribution wherever the
data or its derivatives appear.

Four source-terms questions remain open and must be resolved before any derived
dataset is published. They are listed in docs/adr/0044-licence-and-publication-
policy.md (REQ-1111). No data of any kind is present in this repository at the
time of first commit.
